[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3818640229","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3818640229","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3818640229,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jm9Nl","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T16:06:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T16:25:07Z","body":"I'm guessing that the \"Apple Software Renderer\" being chosen as the device for the compatibility renderer is likely the problem, seeing as how Metal works fine with its \"Apple Paravirtual device\".\n\nIf we assume there's no quick fix for accommodating for this software renderer (which I haven't looked into) would it maybe make sense to have the project manager default to Forward+ on macOS in general, instead of OpenGL?\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5ad8b27d8db0776700c2b08bf68fbea5e0a4680d/main/main.cpp#L2428-L2433","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3818640229/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819122690","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3819122690","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3819122690,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jozAC","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T17:19:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T17:19:45Z","body":"> If we assume there's no quick fix for accommodating for this software renderer (which I haven't looked into) would it maybe make sense to have the project manager default to Forward+ on macOS in general, instead of OpenGL?\n\nPotentially, my only concerns are startup time and non Apple Silicon Macs. We moved to OpenGL both because of compatibility with the broadest range of devices, but also because it starts up significantly faster. That may not be true on Macos these days, so could be reconsidered. \n\nI would measure both startup time and check how effective the fallback is from Forward+ to compatibility when using an older Intel mac","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819122690/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819703467","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3819703467","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3819703467,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7jrAyr","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-29T19:01:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T19:01:32Z","body":"In terms of startup time, I did a quick test on Linux (AMD Radeon 780M) with `hyperfine -w3 -r10 \"Godot_v4.6-stable_linux.x86_64 --rendering-driver vulkan\" \"Godot_v4.6-stable_linux.x86_64 --rendering-driver opengl3\"` and I actually get a slightly faster start time with Vulkan (I did multiple runs of 10 tests, ranging from \"1.06 ± 0.03 times faster\" to \"1.11 ± 0.09 times faster\").\n\nThis is with a pre-existing shader cache, first Vulkan run without cache is slightly slower (1.1s with cache, 1.4s without).\n\nShould definitely be tested on Windows and macOS too, I suspect the gains on Windows might be bigger.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3819703467/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3823749720","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3823749720","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3823749720,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j6cpY","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T13:27:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T13:42:06Z","body":"macOS 26.2, M1 Max, 32GB; `godot master (80a4af1)`\n\n### Blank Project\n\nHot caches:\n\n```\nSummary\n  godot --editor --quit Games/blank/project.godot --rendering-driver metal ran\n    1.05 ± 0.05 times faster than godot --editor --quit Games/blank/project.godot --rendering-driver vulkan\n    1.06 ± 0.05 times faster than godot --editor --quit Games/blank/project.godot --rendering-driver opengl3\n```\n\nCleared caches via `hyperfine --prepare`\n```\nSummary\n  godot --editor --quit Games/blank/project.godot --rendering-driver opengl3 ran\n    1.07 ± 0.05 times faster than godot --editor --quit Games/blank/project.godot --rendering-driver metal\n    1.09 ± 0.06 times faster than godot --editor --quit Games/blank/project.godot --rendering-driver vulkan\n```\n\n### Project Manager\nHot cache:\n```\nSummary\n  godot --quit --project-manager --rendering-driver metal ran\n    1.06 ± 0.01 times faster than godot --quit --project-manager --rendering-driver vulkan\n    1.06 ± 0.01 times faster than godot --quit --project-manager --rendering-driver opengl3\n```\n\nClear cache:\n```\nSummary\n  godot --quit --project-manager --rendering-driver opengl3 ran\n    1.22 ± 0.04 times faster than godot --quit --project-manager --rendering-driver vulkan\n    1.27 ± 0.04 times faster than godot --quit --project-manager --rendering-driver metal\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3823749720/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3823914712","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3823914712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3823914712,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j7E7Y","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T14:01:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T14:01:05Z","body":"Looking at the [minimum system requirements](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/about/system_requirements.html) for Godot, I assume we'd be forced to bump the minimum macOS version from 10.13 (High Sierra) to 10.15 (Catalina) if we went with Forward+ for the project manager? How much of a problem would that be?\n\nI should also note that it's possible to detect a UTM environment (and maybe `Virtualization.framework` environments in general?) through `OS::get_model_name()`, which seems to return `VirtualMac2,1`. So we could also just add a special case for these virtualized environments somewhere. I don't know whether that would cover all the other kinds of virtual machines though, but we also don't know if they suffer from the same problem.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3823914712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824003520","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824003520","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824003520,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j7anA","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T14:16:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T14:16:17Z","body":"> Looking at the [minimum system requirements](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/about/system_requirements.html) for Godot, I assume we'd be forced to bump the minimum macOS version from 10.13 (High Sierra) to 10.15 (Catalina) if we went with Forward+ for the project manager? How much of a problem would that be?\n\nOnly macOS 14.0+ are supported by Apple and receiving security updates. So dropping support for older versions should not be a big issue.\n\nIf we want to switch to Metal as default, the editor will probably need to bundle baked shaders (`.metallib`), otherwise first start can be pretty slow.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824003520/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824028481","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824028481","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824028481,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j7gtB","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T14:21:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T14:21:45Z","body":"For the reference Godot 4.6 compatibility renderer runs fine in macOS 15.7.3 and macOS 12.7.6 UTM virtual machines (running on M4 Pro mac), so seems like something is broken in macOS 26 specifically (OpenGL in VM was broken in early macOS 26 betas, and likely was never fixed, since OpenGL on macOS is deprecated).","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824028481/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824059062","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824059062","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824059062,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j7oK2","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T14:28:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T14:34:18Z","body":"I decided to also give Vulkan/MoltenVK a try in UTM (on Tahoe), and while that does start, it looks to be pretty borked:\n\n<img width=\"1264\" height=\"912\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ed885f39-96d0-45f8-8851-6f26400fb136\" />\n\n(This applies to both Forward+ and Mobile.)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824059062/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824100670","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824100670","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824100670,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j7yU-","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T14:38:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T14:38:03Z","body":"Also, it's not VM issue, but Apple Software Renderer issue. If you force it by adding `NSOpenGLPFARendererID, kCGLRendererGenericFloatID` to the pixel format attributes, it will crash with the same trace on host macOS 26.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824100670/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824163007","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824163007","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824163007,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j8Bi_","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T14:52:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T14:52:14Z","body":"> Looking at the [minimum system requirements](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/about/system_requirements.html) for Godot, I assume we'd be forced to bump the minimum macOS version from 10.13 (High Sierra) to 10.15 (Catalina) if we went with Forward+ for the project manager? How much of a problem would that be?\n\nWe should have a fallback from Metal/Vulkan to OpenGL which I assume works, so this shouldn't be required. We could also likely use some `@available` check to keep the OpenGL default on < 10.15.\n\nI do think it can make sense to bump our min support macOS version, but I don't think this issue is a good justification for it in itself. So that should be considered for its own merits IMO.\n\n> If we want to switch to Metal as default, the editor will probably need to bundle baked shaders (.metallib), otherwise first start can be pretty slow.\n\nAssuming @mieko cleaned up the baked shaders in the cold test above (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3823749720), the difference doesn't seem too drastic, so if it's just for the first start it's probably not worth bundling what's probably several MBs of shaders.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824163007/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824201477","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824201477","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824201477,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j8K8F","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T15:01:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T15:07:45Z","body":"> Assuming mieko cleaned up the baked shaders in the cold test above (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3823749720), the difference doesn't seem too drastic\n\nIt doesn't answer @clayjohn's concern about Intel-based machines though, which I take it would have different characteristics, assuming they're worth catering to in the first place. Those will likely be relevant for a few more years. I don't have one to test with myself though.\n\nEDIT: Re-reading his comment, I may have misunderstood it. Maybe it was just about the fallback for Intel-based machines?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824201477/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824292438","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824292438","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824292438,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j8hJW","user":{"login":"mieko","id":364079,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2NDA3OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/364079?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko","html_url":"https://github.com/mieko","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mieko/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T15:22:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T15:26:26Z","body":"> Assuming @mieko cleaned up the baked shaders in the cold test above (https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3823749720), the difference doesn't seem too drastic\n\nThe script I have that clears the shader cache to simulate first launch for my game removes:\n\n```\n${PROJECT}/.godot/shader_cache\n${HOME}/Library/Application Support/Godot/shader_cache\n${HOME}/Library/Application Support/Godot/app_userdata/${PROJECT_NAME}/shader_cache\n```\n\n(It cleared the editor cache anyway, because I build the editor very often, and it gets crowded with new hashes.)\n\nIt does not clear any low-level system caches (e.g., `$(getconf DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR)/com.apple.metal`, or any analogues for OpenGL and MoltenVK).  I'm not sure if they'd come into play, or where they live if they do.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824292438/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824340087","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824340087","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824340087,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j8sx3","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T15:33:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T15:33:24Z","body":"Maybe a bit hasty of me, but I took the liberty of opening a pull request for changing the project manager to Forward+ on macOS: #115635","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824340087/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824394853","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115580#issuecomment-3824394853","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/115580","id":3824394853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7j86Jl","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T15:46:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T15:46:20Z","body":"> We should have a fallback from Metal/Vulkan to OpenGL which I assume works, so this shouldn't be required.\n\nBut not the other way. We can add fallback from GL to Metal/Vulkan and add `NSOpenGLPFAAccelerated` to GL attributes, which will cause GL context creation to fail if only software renderer is available. This should be sufficient to fix VM issue.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3824394853/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]